{"skill":{"slug":"lead-enrichment-skill","displayName":"Lead Enrichment Skill"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1778619833672,"changelog":"Initial release of lead-enrichment skill.\n\n- Enriches company or person leads using public web signals via Prismfy.\n- Produces a fit verdict (fit, likely_fit, weak_fit, not_fit, ambiguous) with key facts, red flags, and optional structured JSON output.\n- Supports enrichment and qualification before outreach, surfacing disqualifiers and handling ambiguity.\n- Integrates with openclaw, requires PRISMFY_API_KEY, curl, and jq.\n- Includes clear setup instructions, command examples, output formats, and failure handling guidance.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":430,"sha256":"67865bbba3e99a74a8f45354033e1ab04e8c2c884bdee20feab8e037b8484588","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"lead-enrich.sh","size":22773,"sha256":"cef6fe33ab53ae4017e411c24f2e0489ef6703c48cb312aad76bd61a3bff9e53","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"README.md","size":3603,"sha256":"b7cb00265aed82608a8a4529569f5f66e334c6a19cc9ec6c5ab466f97bd7a6df","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8534,"sha256":"2fc395eb58481a900228f8cfc0979e18a5e9e27d772675b25a5976360bf3dd42","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hooks/lead-enrichment/handler.js","size":1533,"sha256":"256ba26b517d7174185330f22b0f1f2360930e0c5a85e9d4283bc9fd5d8ac7d5","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"hooks/lead-enrichment/HOOK.md","size":339,"sha256":"1047814c0c11e618c91dc739d6c1ff56fad066204f0fa12449432f82e0363c78","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2224,"sha256":"08752564db4eed908560ce545bf6353410029932805f13f8ff9df51ca2a1cc78","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789546732734,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b94db8214c4add30fd72c0e6d894664078fff9eb013999bd5d21f7b76795cabb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b94db8214c4add30fd72c0e6d894664078fff9eb013999bd5d21f7b76795cabb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780087550803},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":77,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789546732734},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed lead-enrichment helper that sends user-provided lead queries to Prismfy and optionally saves reports or installs a reminder hook.","dimensions":[{"detail":"curl, jq, network access, and a Prismfy API key are proportionate to the search/enrichment purpose; custom endpoint variables are documented but not validated before credentials are sent.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is ordinary for an OpenClaw skill; setup includes a user-directed option to append the Prismfy API key to ~/.bashrc, which is disclosed but stores the secret in plaintext.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions give clear use and non-use cases, but Prismfy should be understood as receiving lead names, company details, ICP terms, and related query metadata.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Persistence is limited to user-directed shell-profile API-key storage and an optional bootstrap reminder hook; I found no hidden service, scheduler, backdoor, or destructive persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, metadata, README, SKILL.md, helper script, and hook all align around public-web lead enrichment and qualification using Prismfy.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending lead-enrichment queries to Prismfy. Prefer setting PRISMFY_API_KEY only for the session or via a dedicated secret manager rather than storing it in ~/.bashrc, avoid custom endpoint variables unless you trust the exact HTTPS host, and keep exported JSON reports out of shared folders or source control.","findings":"[YR1] expected: The matched text is a documented command to persist PRISMFY_API_KEY in ~/.bashrc, not SSH injection, a hidden user, or a backdoor payload.\n[LP3] expected: The shell helper uses bash, curl, and jq for its documented local CLI workflow; metadata declares the required environment variable and binaries, though it lacks a narrow command permission contract.\n[SQP-2] expected: Credential setup and optional JSON export are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but users should treat both the shell-profile key and saved lead reports as sensitive local data.\n[SDI-2] expected: The hook injects only a virtual reminder about the documented lead-enrichment workflow and does not itself read credentials or run network calls.\n[E1] expected: Authenticated external transmission to Prismfy is the core search mechanism, not hidden exfiltration; the main residual issue is that endpoint override variables can redirect credentials if the environment is already influenced.\n[T09] unexpected: The unrestricted PRISMFY_API_URL, PRISMFY_API_ROOT, and PRISMFY_ME_URL overrides are a real hardening issue because the bearer token is sent to the configured destination without scheme or host validation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789546732734}}}}}